Since students are generally fond of criticism, the blog writer strives to improve his writing in order to avoid criticism.
Blogging also forces students to become more familiar with the world around them. The need to generate interest among readers (listeners) motivates students to be alert and interesting (Toto, 2004).
Blogging is a tool that encourages collaboration and promotes skills for students to learn more effectively beyond traditional school days.
