Kruger National Park (KNP) is located in the northeastern part of South Africa, stretching from the border with Mozambique in the east, northward to Zimbabwe, and southward to the Limpopo River.
This park covers an area of 19,500 kilometers and is divided into 14 different ecological zones, each of which is suitable for a distinct wildlife.
